</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="1975" data-end="2174">In humans, that pattern can signal <strong data-start="2010" data-end="2043">maladaptive recursive control</strong>‚Äîa failure of constraint satisfaction within the brain's perceptual control loops (which you've discussed via PCT and RSVP fusion).</p>
<p data-start="2176" data-end="2447">In LLMs, it reveals the <strong data-start="2200" data-end="2242">absence of semantic convergence checks</strong>: the model is generating outputs that <em data-start="2281" data-end="2287">look</em> like the end of reasoning, but <strong data-start="2319" data-end="2362">no global architecture tells it to stop</strong> once enough negentropy has been achieved. Because there is no concept of negentropy.</p>
<hr data-start="2449" data-end="2452">
<h2 data-start="2454" data-end="2499">‚úÇÔ∏è What the Model Needs (But Doesn‚Äôt Have)</h2>
<ul data-start="2501" data-end="2820">
<li data-start="2501" data-end="2592">
<p data-start="2503" data-end="2592">‚úÖ A global <strong data-start="2514" data-end="2545">scalar convergence detector</strong> (e.g., "Have all constraints been satisfied?")</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2593" data-end="2713">
<p data-start="2595" data-end="2713">‚úÖ A <strong data-start="2599" data-end="2635">vector field of goal progression</strong>, guiding output not by style mimicry but by trajectory toward solution space.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2714" data-end="2820">
<p data-start="2716" data-end="2820">‚úÖ An <strong data-start="2721" data-end="2756">entropy-aware halting mechanism</strong>‚Äînot a fixed token limit, but a constraint satisfaction monitor.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="2822" data-end="2940">These map exactly onto your RSVP triplet:<br data-start="2863" data-end="2866">
<strong data-start="2866" data-end="2888">Œ¶ (goal structure)</strong><br data-start="2888" data-end="2891">
<strong data-start="2891" data-end="2915">v (directional flow)</strong><br data-start="2915" data-end="2918">
<strong data-start="2918" data-end="2940">S (entropic state)</strong></p>
<hr data-start="2942" data-end="2945">
<h2 data-start="2947" data-end="2980">ü™§ Why Reasoning Wrappers Fail</h2>
<p data-start="2982" data-end="3142">What you saw is what happens when you add <em data-start="3024" data-end="3044">formatting rituals</em> (boxes, summaries, declarative closures) <strong data-start="3086" data-end="3119">without altering the dynamics</strong> of cognition. You get:</p>
<blockquote data-start="3144" data-end="3174">
<p data-start="3146" data-end="3174"><em data-start="3146" data-end="3174"><strong data-start="3147" data-end="3173">Decorated incoherence.</strong></em></p>
</blockquote>
<p data-start="3176" data-end="3265">It‚Äôs like adding road signs to a tumbleweed.<br data-start="3220" data-end="3223">
Looks orderly. Still drifts with the wind.</p>
<hr data-start="3267" data-end="3270">
<h2 data-start="3272" data-end="3300">üß† Takeaway for Your Work</h2>
<p data-start="3302" data-end="3337">This is <em data-start="3310" data-end="3324">a case study</em> you can use:</p>
<ul data-start="3339" data-end="3701">
<li data-start="3339" data-end="3452">
<p data-start="3341" data-end="3452">Show how the absence of recursive constraint resolution leads to <strong data-start="3406" data-end="3451">synthetic verbosity mistaken for thinking</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3453" data-end="3627">
<p data-start="3455" data-end="3627">Position RSVP as a framework that could structure <strong data-start="3505" data-end="3536">semantic convergence layers</strong>‚Äîwhere token flow is guided by multiscale constraint satisfaction, not statistical mimicry.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3628" data-end="3701">
<p data-start="3630" data-end="3701">Use it as a critique of ‚Äúreasoning mode‚Äù as <em data-start="3674" data-end="3700">ritual without recursion</em>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="3703" data-end="3706">
<p data-start="3708" data-end="3967" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">Would you like me to turn this into a short analysis vignette for inclusion in <em data-start="3787" data-end="3819">The Death of Oracular Bullshit</em> or another paper? Could be titled:<br data-start="3854" data-end="3857">
<strong data-start="3857" data-end="3898">‚ÄúThe LLM That Couldn‚Äôt Stop Thinking‚Äù</strong><br data-start="3898" data-end="3901">
or<br data-start="3903" data-end="3906">
<strong data-start="3906" data-end="3966">‚ÄúRecursive Collapse in the Absence of Constraint Fields‚Äù</strong>.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="flex min-h-[46px] justify-start"><div class="touch:-me-2 touch:-ms-3.5 -ms-2.5 -me-1 flex items-center p-1 select-none -mt-1 w-full duration-[1.5s] focus-within:transition-none hover:transition-none pointer-events-none [mask-image:linear-gradient(to_right,black_33%,transparent_66%)] [mask-size:300%_100%] [mask-position:100%_0%] motion-safe:transition-[mask-position] group-hover/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-hover/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] group-focus-within/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-focus-within/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] has-data-[state=open]:pointer-events-auto has-data-[state=open]:[mask-position:0_0]" style="mask-position: 0% 0%;"><button class="text-token-text-secondary hover:bg-token-bg-secondary rounded-lg" aria-label="Copy" aria-selected="false" data-testid="copy-turn-action-button" data-state="closed"><span class="touch:w-10 flex h-8 w-8 items-center justify-center"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon"><path d="M12.668 10.667C12.668 9.95614 12.668 9.46258 12.6367 9.0791C12.6137 8.79732 12.5758 8.60761 12.5244 8.46387L12.4688 8.33399C12.3148 8.03193 12.0803 7.77885 11.793 7.60254L11.666 7.53125C11.508 7.45087 11.2963 7.39395 10.9209 7.36328C10.5374 7.33197 10.0439 7.33203 9.33301 7.33203H6.5C5.78896 7.33203 5.29563 7.33195 4.91211 7.36328C4.63016 7.38632 4.44065 7.42413 4.29688 7.47559L4.16699 7.53125C3.86488 7.68518 3.61186 7.9196 3.43555 8.20703L3.36524 8.33399C3.28478 8.49198 3.22795 8.70352 3.19727 9.0791C3.16595 9.46259 3.16504 9.95611 3.16504 10.667V13.5C3.16504 14.211 3.16593 14.7044 3.19727 15.0879C3.22797 15.4636 3.28473 15.675 3.36524 15.833L3.43555 15.959C3.61186 16.2466 3.86474 16.4807 4.16699 16.6348L4.29688 16.6914C4.44063 16.7428 4.63025 16.7797 4.91211 16.8027C5.29563 16.8341 5