#### 1. Formalizing the NDS Algorithm in Pseudocode

The **Negentropic Directional Solver (NDS)** can be formalized as a loop-based algorithm that applies directional flow rules to disks within the three-pole system. Below is a pseudocode representation:

<pre class="overflow-x-auto"><code>pseudocode
// Negentropic Directional Solver for Tower of Hanoi
// Input: n disks, 3 poles (source, auxiliary, target), initial configuration
// Output: Sequence of moves to achieve goal state (all disks on target pole)

initialize:
  poles = {source: [1, 2, ..., n], auxiliary: [], target: []} // Disks numbered 1 (smallest) to n (largest)
  directions = {disk_i: "left" if disk_i is large else "right"} // Assign directions based on size
  valid_moves = {(pole_i, pole_j): allowed if top disk on pole_i &lt; top disk on pole_j or pole_j is empty}

while not goal_state(poles): // All disks on target pole in order
  // Identify movable disks (top disks on each pole)
  movable_disks = get_top_disks(poles)
  
  // Select smallest movable disk
  current_disk = min(movable_disks)
  current_pole = get_pole_of_disk(current_disk)
  
  // Determine target pole based on directional flow
  target_pole = get_next_pole(current_pole, directions[current_disk])
  
  // Validate and execute move
  if is_valid_move(current_pole, target_pole):
    move_disk(current_disk, current_pole, target_pole)
  else:
    // Skip to next iteration or adjust flow if blocked
    continue
  
  // Update pole states
  update_poles(poles)

// Helper functions
function get_next_pole(current_pole, direction):
  if direction == "left":
    return (current_pole - 1) mod 3 // Cyclic: left -&gt; center -&gt; right -&gt; left
  else:
    return (current_pole + 1) mod 3 // Cyclic: right -&gt; center -&gt; left -&gt; right

function goal_state(poles):
  return poles.target == [1, 2, ..., n] and poles.source == [] and poles.auxiliary == []</code></pre>

**Key Features**:
- The algorithm prioritizes the smallest movable disk to ensure progress (a standard Tower of Hanoi constraint).
- Directional flows are defined modulo 3, reflecting the cyclic pole topology.
- The system iterates until the goal state is reached, with local moves guided by the vector field (directions).

